    <string name="external_control_sub">Lets broadcasts and Tasker drive Waypoint</string>
    <string name="detect_body">Android marks every fix from a mock provider with an isMock flag. Apps that read it can refuse to work — banking, ride-hailing and some games do. Waypoint does not hide the flag: doing so needs root and breaks a guarantee other apps rely on.\n\nRandom jitter and a realistic altitude make readings look natural, but they never remove the flag.</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Waypoint has no account, no analytics and no network access beyond fetching map tiles. Favourites and routes stay on this device. Nothing about where you are — or pretend to be — ever leaves it.</string>
